// Reducer for the head-colon spin class: a ':' HEADING an expression
// parse has no owner (every legal ':' — ternary, case label, range-for,
// label, bitfield — consumes a left side first), and the old pushback
// handed the SAME token back to the caller's loop forever. The original
// reducer shape (`m = { "a": 1 };`) became LEGAL when assignment-rhs
// carrier literals landed (owner 2026-08-31), so the wall is now pinned
// through a keyed element MISSING its key — the ':' heads the element's
// own expression parse. Must ERROR, never hang.
// Oracle: g++ `v = {: 2};` -> "expected primary-expression before ':'".
int main()
{
	var m = { : 1 };
	return 0;
}
